Give a hosted plugin room to write a MIDI key name.

FST (the clean-room header this code compiles against, see CMakeLists.txt)
declares MidiKeyName's keyName[] as a flexible array, where Steinberg's
header declares keyName[kVstMaxNameLen]. With FST the struct holds the two
leading ints and no name at all: MSVC refuses to value-initialise it
(error C2466, "cannot allocate an array of constant size 0"), and GCC/Clang
accepted it while effGetMidiKeyName wrote the plugin's answer past the
struct into the stack. The struct now sits at the start of a zeroed buffer
with room for the whole name; field offsets are the same under either header.
diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormatImpl.h b/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormatImpl.h
index 71bfe5d..ba1a689 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormatImpl.h
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTPluginFormatImpl.h
@@ -1321,7 +1321,13 @@ struct VSTPluginInstanceHeadless : public AudioPluginInstance,
 
     std::optional<String> getNameForMidiNoteNumber (int note, int midiChannel) override
     {
-        Vst2::MidiKeyName keyName{};
+        // PLECTRIFY_VST2_MIDI_KEY_NAME_STORAGE: FST declares keyName[] as a
+        // flexible array, so the struct itself holds no name at all: MSVC refuses
+        // to value-initialise it (C2466), and elsewhere the plugin's answer was
+        // written past the struct into the stack. Reserve the name's full length
+        // behind the two leading ints; the offsets are the same under either header.
+        alignas (Vst2::MidiKeyName) char keyNameStorage[sizeof (Vst2::MidiKeyName) + 256] {};
+        auto& keyName = *reinterpret_cast<Vst2::MidiKeyName*> (keyNameStorage);
 
         keyName.thisProgramIndex = getCurrentProgram();
         keyName.thisKeyNumber = note;
